ned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T17:04:29-07:00","id":1234448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1234436#post1234436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zourark? Malamar</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> How would those fit, though?<br /> <br /> I suggested Drowzee and Darkrai, because they have power over dreams, which could be used to keep magical secrets out of the hands of the unworthy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T17:42:37-07:00","id":1234461,"title":"","content":"Zourarock can use illusion and disguise themselves as other people","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T13:53:33-07:00","id":1235328,"title":"","content":"Unrelated to all of this, I'ma let you finish, but Arcanine is the best Pokemon of all time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T15:10:29-07:00","id":1235350,"title":"","content":"I just wanna say I wish that the posibility of sending pokemons from go to the main game stays in the future and isnt only a thing from Pokemon let\u00b4s go.<br /> <br /> It would make more interesting to fill the dex and to make the team you want without overloading the region with non regional pokes after all discovering the new biodiversity of a region is a great part of the fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T20:34:55-07:00","id":1235408,"title":"","content":"You're a gym leader. Four Pok\u00e9mon all of the same type. What is your theme and which ones do you use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T21:53:30-07:00","id":1235423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1235408#post1235408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're a gym leader. Four Pok\u00e9mon all of the same type. What is your theme and which ones do you use?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, good question! With those constraints, I think I'll go with ice. Alolan Ninetails, Alolan Sandslash, Froslass, and Dewgong (Glalie would be a better fit, but I hate it). Gimmick is obviously hail, with the full suite of Snow Warning, Slush Rush, Snow Cloak, and Ice Body. Though, I'm also tempted to drop the Dewgong for Weavile because it's one of my favorite pokemon.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I might go fire, with Alolan Marrowak, Salazzle, Volcarona, and Talonflame. No particular theme there, just four same-type pokemon from the same region that I like a lot.<br /> <br /> But evidently I'd be in the Alola region either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T22:06:30-07:00","id":1235426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1235408#post1235408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're a gym leader. Four Pok\u00e9mon all of the same type. What is your theme and which ones do you use?</div> </div> </div> </div>My theme is Victory Through Attrition, and my Pokemon are of the Poison Type.<br /> <br /> I use:<br /> <br /> Grimer/Muk - For spamming debuffs and generic poison attacks.<br /> <br /> Venonat/Venomoth -.For the additional off-type powers and the extra poison attacks. They'd be my default fight ender using surprise finishes.<br /> <br /> Nidoran/Nidoking - The emergency heavy hitter. Likely having learned Megahorn and Earthquake at higher levels.<br /> <br /> Oddish/Vileplume - The unexpected tank. Using Absorb and the various Absorb, Only Better powers makes keeping them standing in a fight easier than normal. Add to that Leech Seed and Moonlight, and you have a Pokemon who just keeps coming. My ideal combination, if I had to pair it down to the classic 4 moves per Pokemon, would be Mega Drain, Leech Seed, Moonlight and Solarbeam. Mechanically speaking, those last two used together are a fun combination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 07-16-2018, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T22:08:11-07:00","id":1235427,"title":"","content":"Steel Type - Scizor, Agislash, Metagross, Empoleon<br /> <br /> Theme is roughly adapt or die. These four have lots of resistances and no one type weakness across all four. No blitzing with a single mon for you! (Although I'm sure there's something that could get a move for each weakness. But you get my point)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 07-16-2018, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T22:29:59-07:00","id":1235438,"title":"","content":"I am obliged to say Dark, because seriously, no one has been a Dark type Gym Leader, but instead they have been unfairly cast as the go-to for criminal organizations. Well no more I say!<br /> <br /> Dark-type, Two-pokemon team style battles.<br /> <br /> Houndoom<br /> Honchcrow<br /> Sharpedo<br /> Krookodile<br /> <br /> Yes, they are all dual types, still, I am a dual-type kind of guy.<br /> <br /> Gonna have to think on theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-16-2018, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T22:31:05-07:00","id":1235440,"title":"","content":"On the subject of themed teams, ever since the addition of fairy type, I\u2019ve wanted a fantasy-themed elite four. Fairy, dragon, steel, and poison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T22:32:51-07:00","id":1235441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1235438#post1235438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they are all dual types, still, I am a dual-type kind of guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dual-type is the only way to go! Gotta get that type chart coverage. My current six-mon team without same-type or same-region restriction would be Alolan Marrowak, Weavile, Mawile, Breloom, Kingdra, and Crobat. My only regrets are that I don\u2019t have room for anything with psychic type and that I\u2019m just shy of a full team of two-stage lines.<br /> <br /> Of course, with my name I\u2019m obviously destined to become a professor in the Pok\u00e9mon universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-16-2018, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T22:39:34-07:00","id":1235446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1235441#post1235441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dual-type is the only way to go! Gotta get that type chart coverage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, really, if I were a gym-leader I'd ignore the type-casting and just min-max the fuck out of dual-type advantage. The only pokemon I would ever have on my team that is single type is the afore mentioned Best Pokemon Arcanine.<br /> <br /> I think back in the Crystal days my team was Houndoom, Heracross, Ivysaur, Slowking, Magneton, and Dragonite. Haven't perfectly crafted a team for X yet.<br /> <br /> EDIT: With MY name I would have to not be a Pokemon trainer because I am not letting my name consign me to my fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-16-2018, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T23:01:34-07:00","id":1235455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1235446#post1235446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> With MY name I would have to not be a Pokemon trainer because I am not letting my name consign me to my fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... in my case it\u2019s a chosen name and actually the thing I would want to do in the Pok\u00e9mon universe, so that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T07:55:24-07:00","id":1235558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1235441#post1235441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dual-type is the only way to go! Gotta get that type chart coverage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah, all you need is a Feraligatr and you're covered for just about anything.<br /> <br /> <b>Move Set I used:</b><br /> <br /> Superpower (fighting)<br /> <br /> Crunch (dark)<br /> <br /> Ice Fang (ice)<br /> <br /> Hydro Cannon (water)<br /> <br /> <br /> With the exception of Red and the need for HM slaves, I used that build to solo my way through Soul Silver!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-16-2018, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T09:25:51-07:00","id":1235583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1235558#post1235558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, all you need is a Feraligatr and you're covered for just about anything.<br /> <br /> <b>Move Set I used:</b><br /> <br /> Superpower (fighting)<br /> <br /> Crunch (dark)<br /> <br /> Ice Fang (ice)<br /> <br /> Hydro Cannon (water)<br /> <br /> <br /> With the exception of Red and the need for HM slaves, I used that build to solo my way through Soul Silver!</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, obviously you want to build your Pok\u00e9mon\u2019s movesets to have good type coverage. But building your team to also have a good type spread means STAB on more of your coverage moves. Plus, there\u2019s just so many cool types! I always try to have a ghost, a flying, and a poison type on my team if I can help it. I also place high priority on dragon, fairy, steel, dark, and psychic. Then of course, you\u2019ve got to get that grass/water/fire triangle in there if you can. Fighting and Ice are very useful to have. There are just too many cool types not to double-up as much as possible!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T11:28:11-07:00","id":1235647,"title":"","content":"In spite of my earlier statement, one of my favorite Types has always been Ghost, but it really irked me that the only three we had in the first generation were <i>also</i> Poison-types, and thus super vulnerable to Psychics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T11:40:11-07:00","id":1235659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1235647#post1235647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In spite of my earlier statement, one of my favorite Types has always been Ghost, but it really irked me that the only three we had in the first generation were <i>also</i> Poison-types, and thus super vulnerable to Psychics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always found it odd in the anime when Sabrina\u2019s dad was like \u201cyou need a ghost type Pok\u00e9mon to defeat her!\u201d Like, it worked, but only because battles were calvinball in the first season.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T19:42:57-07:00","id":1235780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1235659#post1235659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always found it odd in the anime when Sabrina\u2019s dad was like \u201cyou need a ghost type Pok\u00e9mon to defeat her!\u201d Like, it worked, but only because battles were calvinball in the first season.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was playing gen one during the first broadcast of the anime and so many of us tried to take tips on playing the game from the show. It basically never worked out well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T19:45:07-07:00","id":1235781,"title":"","content":"I think I'd be a fossil gym leader. Rock-type. <br /> <br /> Omastar, Kabutops, Cradily, and Aerodactyl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T20:34:36-07:00","id":1235788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1235780#post1235780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was playing gen one during the first broadcast of the anime and so many of us tried to take tips on playing the game from the show. It basically never worked out well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, no duh. The show doesn't adhere to gameplay mechanics. There have been several instances in the anime where they completely ignore type advantages, such as electric attacks being able to affect ground type pokemon.<br /> <br /> In fact, the manga is guilty of this, too. Since Red's pikachu killed Brock's onix by blowing it up with a thunder bolt!<br /> <br /> Kind of makes Ash's pikachu look like a weak scrub, by comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T20:45:19-07:00","id":1235792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1235788#post1235788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, no duh. The show doesn't adhere to gameplay mechanics. There have been several instances in the anime where they completely ignore type advantages, such as electric attacks being able to affect ground type pokemon.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is obvious now, but in 1999 from the perspective of a bunch of ten year olds why <i>wouldn't</i> the anime be a reliable source for information on the game? Pretty much all of our knowledge of the game was folk-wisdom absorbed through our own parsing of the game's rules as we played it, dog-eared pages of the one strategy guide that got passed around at recess, angelfire and geocities sites on dial-up internet, then the 6 AM anime. It was a weird and wooly time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T21:07:15-07:00","id":1235799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1235792#post1235792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is obvious now, but in 1999 from the perspective of a bunch of ten year olds why <i>wouldn't</i> the anime be a reliable source for information on the game? Pretty much all of our knowledge of the game was folk-wisdom absorbed through our own parsing of the game's rules as we played it, dog-eared pages of the one strategy guide that got passed around at recess, angelfire and geocities sites on dial-up internet, then the 6 AM anime. It was a weird and wooly time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, some of my friends <i>still</i> go into weird button-mashing frenzies when throwing Pok\u00e9balls!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T21:23:22-07:00","id":1235803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1235780#post1235780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was playing gen one during the first broadcast of the anime and so many of us tried to take tips on playing the game from the show. It basically never worked out well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was playing at that time too, but I just relied on my massively over-leveled blastoise for everything.<br /> <br /> I really wanted a Pikachu and I knew I could find them in Viridian forest, so I spent a huge amount of time there. I was also really bad at judging how much damage I could safely do before trying to catch wild Pokemon, so I kept accidently KOing things, until my squirtle was one-shotting all the Pikachu I was trying to catch. When I finally gave up on trying to catch one, I had a wartortle, and that pretty much carried me through the rest of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T21:25:54-07:00","id":1235804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1235799#post1235799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, some of my friends <i>still</i> go into weird button-mashing frenzies when throwing Pok\u00e9balls!</div> </div> </div> </div>In my school it was &quot;hold up and b.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T02:47:55-07:00","id":1235849,"title":"","content":"I remember catching a Dewgong at recess on my original gameboy and the other kids being impressed by my unquestionable awesomeness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> I also remember not noticing at the time that Rare Candies in the original release of Red and Blue only increased your level, but did not affect your stats at all. <br /> <br /> The shear amount of confusion and rage I suffered through bringing my cheated level 100 team to battle the Elite Four in Pokemon Stadium, only to watch them get slaughtered by the enemy... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T14:31:50-07:00","id":1236145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1235849#post1235849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also remember not noticing at the time that Rare Candies in the original release of Red and Blue only increased your level, but did not affect your stats at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because rare candies <i>did</i> increase stats. They just didn\u2019t affect EVs, which means the stat increases from leveling up were not as significant as they could have been. You could have fixed that problem with stat boosting items like Protien though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T14:59:31-07:00","id":1236161,"title":"","content":"So fun story from the trenches of early Pokemon. In my fifth grade class a kid actually <i>stole</i> a Mewtwo from another kid. Heisted an actual Pokemon out of a game like they were Team Rocket. He and an accomplice took their mark's Gameboy out of his backpack, hooked up the link cable, and forced a trade.<br /> <br /> Then came trying to explain what had happened to adults. <br /> <br /> &quot;So he stole the Gameboy? Justin give him back his Gameboy.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Nono he stole something out of the game!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;He stole the game?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No! He stole a Pokemon <i>from</i> the game!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;How does that work? Isn't a 'pokomin' just part of the game?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No! It belonged to Sam in the game then Justin stole it!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What did he steal?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A Pokemon!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't understand...&quot;<br /> <br /> We were ten year olds trying to articulate the concept of digital property to parents and teachers who's understanding of digital technology began and ended with doomsday prepping for Y2K.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T15:23:20-07:00","id":1236171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1236145#post1236145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably because rare candies <i>did</i> increase stats. They just didn\u2019t affect EVs, which means the stat increases from leveling up were not as significant as they could have been. You could have fixed that problem with stat boosting items like Protien though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think I remember hearing something about vitamins only working for the first 100 EV's or so. In more recent versions of the game, there's a certain point where it tells me that using a particular vitamin on my pokemon won't have any effect, even if I've never used any vitamins on them before. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T15:31:02-07:00","id":1236173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1233546-let\u2019s-talk-about-pok\u00e9mon?p=1236171#post1236171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I remember hearing something about vitamins only working for the first 100 EV's or so. In more recent versions of the game, there's a certain point where it tells me that using a particular vitamin on my pokemon won't have any effect, even if I've never used any vitamins on them before. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Vitamins increase EVs, and a Pok\u00e9mon can only have 510 EVs total, with a maximum of 252 EVs in any one stat, and vitamins can\u2019t raise an EV above 100. So if you attempt to give a Pok\u00e9mon a vitamin and it says it won\u2019t have an effect, that Pok\u00e9mon is either at 100+ EVs for that stat already, or maxed out on EVs total. EVs are also increases by KOing other Pok\u00e9mon, and a few other methods depending on the generation, so that\u2019s why you sometimes reach that limit without using any vitamins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-17-2018, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}